also suggested a survey for intramuscular hematoma, includ ing
iliopsoas hematoma, when progressive anemia is present in
patients with PERM. Our patient actually did have progressive
anemia ( Figure 2C). Therefore, it can be boldly speculated
that the lumbar muscle abscess is an opportunistic pathogenic
infection based on a hematoma caused by muscle contraction.
This case illustrates that patients with PERM may develop
multiple complications, among which some are unpredictable.
CONCLUSION
The PERM is a rare autoimmune disorder with complex
symptoms. Patients may present an acute and severe disease
course and lead to a variety of complications. Recognizing the
atypical initial presentations of PERM is important for patients
with an acute course for fast recognition and proper treatment s
are essential to prevent irreversible damage.
